<title>USA: Hollinger sees '97 EBITDA doubling - paper.</title>
<headline>Hollinger sees '97 EBITDA doubling - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earnings of Hollinger International Inc before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization should double in 1997, after more than doubling in 1996 to $220.7 million, Conrad Black told Barron's.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we're going to surprise a lot of investors,&quot; Black, who controls the company through his holdings in Hollinger Inc, told the financial weekly.</p>
<p>Hollinger International owns the London Telegraph and the Chicago Sun-Times.</p>
